WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.188
- [Instructor] We're asked
to move the dot to 7/6

00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:06.130
on the number line.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.380
So pause this video.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.410
I can move this dot right over here,

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.140
but I encourage you, pause the video,

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.700
and put your finger on where 7/6 would be

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.290
on the number line.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.730
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.120
So what they're saying is,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.720
is from zero to this
point on the number line

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.270
right over there, that gets us to 1/6.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.010
So each of these spaces are a sixth.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.705
So we go zero, 1/6, 2/6,

00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:35.674
3/6, 4/6, 5/6,

00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:36.507
6/6, 7/6.

00:00:39.088 --> 00:00:40.140
Let me make sure I got that.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.690
So each of these are a sixth.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.810
So we have one, two, three,

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.193
four, five, six, 7/6.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.670
So that's 7/6 on that number line.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.930
Now they have other ways of
getting at the same idea.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.200
For example, they say
which point is at 9/4

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.270
on the number line?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.930
And they ask us to choose one answer,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.960
and we can look at the choices here.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.570
So which choice shows
9/4 on the number line?

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.870
Pause this video and see
if you can pick that.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.960
All right, now let's
look at each of these.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.026
So it looks like in choice,
in this first choice,

00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:22.114
the space between zero and one

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:26.890
is split into one, two,
three, four equal spaces.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.640
So as we go from zero to this next line,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.480
that's a fourth.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.520
And that seems like it keeps going.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.580
So this is 1/4, 2/4, 3/4, 4/4,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.310
5/4, 6/4, 7/4,

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.510
8/4, 9/4 is here.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:45.540
That's what we're looking for.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.360
But the dot is not at 9/4.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.500
It's at 10/4, 11/4, it's at 12/4.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.860
So I don't like choice A.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.910
Let's see, choice B.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:57.190
Let's see what is, let's see,

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.700
we have divided the space
between zero and one

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.830
into one, two, three,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.444
four, five, six equal spaces.

00:02:04.444 --> 00:02:06.487
So each of these are a sixth.

00:02:06.487 --> 00:02:08.430
So to go from zero to one,

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:13.430
you've already gone 6/6,
and then 7/6, 8/6, 9/6.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.800
So this is 9/6, not 9/4.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.710
And so let's look at this last choice.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.280
I'm already feeling like it
should be the answer, but.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.450
We can see that the spaces are the same

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.000
as in our first choice,
so these are each fourths.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.640
Once again I know that because the space

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.650
between zero and one or
any two whole numbers

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.080
is divided into four equal spaces.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.320
So to go from zero to one, you go 4/4,

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.830
and then 5/4, 6/4,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:45.630
7/4, 8/4, and 9/4.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.655
So choice C is definitely looking good.

00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:50.536
Let's do one more example.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.920
So here they say, what fraction is located

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.750
at Point A on the number line?

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.313
Pause this video and see
if you can answer that.

00:02:59.313 --> 00:03:00.880
All right.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.990
So between the whole numbers,

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.740
how many spaces, equal spaces, do we have?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.730
It looks like we have one, two, three,

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.210
four, five, six equal spaces.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.860
So things are divided into sixths.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.350
So 1/6, 2/6, 3/6,

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:21.570
4/6, 5/6, 6/6,

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.170
which is equal to one,

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.510
and then 7/6.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.510
So this is seven over six, just like that,

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.863
and we are done.

